    },
    "instructions": "FigCraft is an interface design tool (Figma-class): pages hold frames, groups, shapes, text, components and instances, with auto layout, styles, variables and prototyping. Coordinates are page units (1 unit = 1 px at 100% zoom), x right and y DOWN. create_node and set_properties take x/y RELATIVE TO THE PARENT (the page when there is no parent, so page coordinates); inspect_document reports both x/y relative to the parent frame (groups don't count) and absoluteBounds in page coordinates. Children of an auto-layout frame are positioned by the layout (set layout, gap, padding, mainAlign, crossAlign, sizingH/sizingV instead). Every menu item, panel action and shortcut is a command: find ids and params with list_commands (use a filter) and run them with run_command, or several as one undo step with batch. Commands act on `ids` when given, else on the selection; new layers become the selection. Colours are \"#RRGGBB\" or \"#RRGGBBAA\". Verify your work: inspect_document / get_node return the layer tree as JSON (check sizes, fills, layout, overrides), and screenshot returns a PNG of the page or of given layers to look at. undo/redo step through history. Resources: figcraft://document, figcraft://node/{id}, figcraft://command/{id}. prompts/list has workflows. Backend: headless (in-process engine session; no window). Files: only these folders may be read: [\"/tmp/vaio-figcraft-test\",\"/tmp/vaio-figcraft-test\"]; written: [\"/tmp/vaio-figcraft-test\"] (any other path is refused).",
